From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brett-Michael Green <brett@bmgvisualtech.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 08:09:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] soc: samsung: gs101-pmu: zuma: allow the Wi-Fi PCIe PHY's
 isolation register

zuma's PCIe PHY for its second controller (the Wi-Fi chip's) is
isolated through PMU offset 0x3ec8, as stock's pcie@13120000 gives it
(pmu-offset). Its PHY driver releases the isolation, so add the register
to zuma's PMU regmap, next to UFS's.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Brett-Michael Green <brett@bmgvisualtech.com>
---
 drivers/soc/samsung/gs101-pmu.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/samsung/gs101-pmu.c b/drivers/soc/samsung/gs101-pmu.c
index 9ee77754d..40e26951c 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/samsung/gs101-pmu.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/samsung/gs101-pmu.c
@@ -344,6 +344,7 @@ const struct exynos_pmu_data gs101_pmu_data = {
 #define ZUMA_HSI0_STATUS		0x2a84
 #define ZUMA_PAD_CTRL_NFC_CLK		0x3e84
 #define ZUMA_PHY_CTRL_UFS		0x3ec0
+#define ZUMA_PHY_CTRL_PCIE1		0x3ec8
 
 static const struct regmap_range zuma_pmu_registers[] = {
 	/* reboot mode */
@@ -359,6 +360,7 @@ static const struct regmap_range zuma_pmu_registers[] = {
 	/* PHY isolation */
 	regmap_reg_range(GS101_PHY_CTRL_USB20, GS101_PHY_CTRL_USB20),
 	regmap_reg_range(ZUMA_PHY_CTRL_UFS, ZUMA_PHY_CTRL_UFS),
+	regmap_reg_range(ZUMA_PHY_CTRL_PCIE1, ZUMA_PHY_CTRL_PCIE1),
 	/* a hint TF-A reads, not a status register: see zuma_pmu_regmap_init() */
 	regmap_reg_range(ZUMA_PMU_INFORM0, ZUMA_PMU_INFORM0),
 	/* Tensor G4's NFC reference clock pad, a clock of clk-exynos-clkout */
